+    \item \textbf{Track refitting and matching.} Electron-track candidates are refitted with a Gaussian-sum filter, in which a mixture of Gaussian components is used to describe radiative energy losses. The refitted tracks are extrapolated to the second layer of the EM calorimeter and matched to clusters using their differences in $\eta$ and $\phi$. If several tracks match the same cluster, the $\Delta R$ between each extrapolated track position and the cluster centre is used together with the pixel and SCT hit variables to rank the tracks.
     \item \textbf{Supercluster formation.} Nearby clusters are added to the seed to recover energy from bremsstrahlung. Additional clusters sharing the matched electron track can be collected over a wider region in $\phi$.
